# Makham 16 · มะขาม 16 — pixel font for dialogue (Thai, Latin, Malay), taller and looser than Makham 12
# Easy Font source (easyfont/1). Copyright 2026 Salahuddin Benno. SIL Open Font License 1.1.
# Thai glyphs drawn by hand on a 9-row body; proportions referenced (not traced) from Noto Sans Thai Looped (OFL).
# Latin, digits and punctuation are Makham 12 glyphs moved to this baseline.
#
# Cell rows 0..21, baseline 18. Tone marks 0-2 (low form 5-7), upper vowels 4-7, Thai body 9-17,
# tall letters (ป ฝ ฟ ฬ) from row 5, lower vowels 19-21. 2 px between letters.
format easyfont/1
id makham-16
name Makham 16
th มะขาม 16
size 16
line 22
baseline 18
spacing 2
space 5
zones tone=0 upper=4 body=9 lower=19 lowshift=5 leftshift=2 lowerdrop=0

